id: pm-web-t0mu
title: "pm-web plan link and unlink routes omit the required step positional, so both always fail with a usage error"
description: "POST and DELETE /api/projects/:projectId/pm/plan/:planId/link build ['plan','link',planId,'--link',id] without the step argument pm plan link/unlink requires, so every call exits 2 and the routes could never have linked anything. The routes now take a step field from the request body and pass it positionally, and reject requests without it with 400 before spawning pm."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: bug,http-semantics,pm-plan
created_at: "2026-10-05T04:46:06.574Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-05T05:08:26.295Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: pi-glm
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T05:08:26.295Z",codex-sol,"Resumed regression suite passes against real HTTP, disposable PostgreSQL, and a scratch pm project (4/4). Preserved the interrupted implementation. Linked-test JSON also needed a single-entry array at the SDK dispatch boundary. Explicit persisted-record and bulk membership assertions pin the behavior."
